    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I found and changed\n\nThe RFC7807 plumbing was already in place: `ExceptionControllerAdvice` returns `ProblemDetail` responses (which Spring serializes as `application/problem+json` with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`) for the 400/409/429 handlers (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `DuplicateIdentityException`/`CityOwnerLimitExceededException`, `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`).\n\nThe real defect the new acceptance test (`coreRejectionIsProblemJson`) exposed was that a rejection that *should* be a 400 was instead coming back as a **500**:\n\n- Posting an owner with no `city` should trip the `@NotNull`/`@NotBlank` constraint \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 problem+json.\n- But the class-level `PostcodeValidator` runs during the same validation pass and called `CityRegions.regionOf(null)`. That method did `Map.of(...).get(null)`, and immutable `Map.of` maps throw a `NullPointerException` on a null key. Hibernate Validator wrapped it as `jakarta.validation.ValidationException`, which fell through to the generic 500 handler.\n\n### Fix\n`src/main/java/.../util/CityRegions.java` \u2014 made `regionOf` null-safe, matching its own Javadoc (\"may be null\" \u2192 returns null):\n\n```java\npublic static String regionOf(String city) {\n    if (city == null) {\n        return null;\n    }\n    return CITY_REGION.get(city);\n}\n```\n\nNow validation completes normally, the missing-`city` constraint fires, and the response is a 400 with an `application/problem+json` body carrying `type`, `title`, `status` (400) and `detail` \u2014 satisfying the specification and all tests.",
